title: Repository import
description: Reads a public GitHub repository and draws it. One node per folder, READMEs as read-only pages, and connections from .subcanvas files like this one.
connects:
  - to: src/lib/sync
    label: writes documents from the server
    description: The importer builds each whiteboard and README as a Yjs document on the server and appends it to document_updates, the same log a browser writes to. Nothing imported is special. It opens, syncs, and nests like anything drawn by hand.
  - to: src/lib/whiteboard
    label: nodes, edges, layout
ignore:
  - __fixtures__
